Among the small odds-ratio studies Y238X is null. The largest study (Fisher 2017, 483 cases) reports hazard ratios above 1, and
including it moves the pooled effect up. **The second CLEC7A effect** is the per-copy effect of the A-G haplotype, the G allele of rs7309123 on the non-Y238X background (A-C is the reference). rs7309123 is a C/G
palindrome, so the strand each study used had to be determined from its control frequencies and the papers themselves; the evidence for each study is in
`data/rs7309123_strand_resolution.csv` and in addendum 16 of the decision record. Studies are graded A to D, and only grades A and B (resolved with at least low-to-medium confidence)
enter the primary estimate.


::: {#tbl-strand .cell tbl-cap='Strand of rs7309123 in each study that reports it. The likelihood ratio compares the study\'s control frequency of the labelled allele with the forward-strand and opposite-strand reference frequencies.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
